 "name": "RootSink",
 "description": "Reproducible C/C++ crashes: each record pairs a sink with a candidate root cause, ordered CWE instances with an evidence category each, the fix and, for executed records, sanitizer logs; most sinks are sanitizer-witnessed. GOLD certifies the sink and its two-sided reproduction, not the root. Record ids keep the working name CHAINFORGE. 3341 records; tiers {'gold': 1954, 'silver': 750, 'gold-upstream': 425, 'bronze': 212}.",
 "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
 "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24068722",
 "citeAs": "@misc{rootsink, title = {{RootSink: Reproducible C/C++ Crashes with Tested Repair Sites}}, author = {Sijwali, Suryansh Singh and Lakshmanan, Achintya and Dodda, Abhiram and Chowdhury, Shaiful and Saha, Suman}, year = {2026}, version = {1.0.8}}",
